# Copy to .dev.vars for `npx wrangler dev` and fill in real values.
# .dev.vars is git-ignored; never commit real secrets.

# AES-256-GCM key used to encrypt provider API keys before they are stored in D1.
# Must be base64 of exactly 32 random bytes. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
# Changing this value makes existing rows undecryptable: re-save the keys afterwards.
SECRETS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=3MA8dqfnN1veywbjKPVE9hDwIq2Ra5TXvsTThon+SEc=

# Authorisation is Cloudflare Access' job, and only part of the app needs it.
#
# Public on purpose: `/tts`, /v1/audio/speech (text to speech) and
# /v1/text/polish (uses the caller's own key).
#
# Behind Access: `/api/*` - it can decrypt the stored Trancy password, spend
# Trancy quota and rewrite provider keys - plus the /transcription and /trancy
# pages if you do not want them public.
#
# Local `wrangler dev` has no Access in front, so everything is reachable
# there, which is fine: it is your own machine.

# This is the only secret the Worker needs. Provider keys (OpenAI / ElevenLabs /
# Google) are entered in the settings panel and stored encrypted in D1 - there is
# no environment fallback for them.
